---
// The playground (#419 (playground)): the visitor drives the small system of
// the site, runs seeds, hunts the planted bug and replays a red seed.
// public/playground.js sends each config to the engine and draws the result;
// it holds no simulation logic.
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";
import { url } from "../../nav";
import runs from "../../runs/home.json";
---
<Doc
  title="Playground"
  description="Run seeds of a small replicated register, hunt its planted bug, and replay the red seed."
  kicker="playground"
  section="playground/"
>
  <p>Three servers keep one value on disk; a client writes it to a quorum and reads it back. Pick the faults,
    the count of servers and the planted bug, then run a seed or hunt for a red one. The network, the disk and
    the clock are simulated in your browser; the same code would run on Tokio.</p>
  <div class="breakout">
    <form class="run play" id="play" aria-label="The config of the run">
      <div class="run-head label"><span>the config</span><span id="play-share"></span></div>
      <div class="play-grid">
        <div class="play-seed">
          <label class="label" for="play-seed">seed</label>
          <input id="play-seed" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="15" autocomplete="off" />
          <button class="btn small" type="button" id="play-next">Next seed</button>
          <button class="btn small" type="button" id="play-random">Random seed</button>
        </div>
        <fieldset class="switches">
          <legend class="label">faults</legend>
          <label><input type="checkbox" id="play-net" /> network</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" id="play-disk" /> storage</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" id="play-reboots" /> reboots</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" id="play-wipes" /> disk wipes</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" id="play-swarm" /> swarm</label>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset class="switches">
          <legend class="label">system</legend>
          <label>servers <select id="play-servers">{[1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((n) => <option value={n}>{n}</option>)}</select></label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" id="play-bug" /> planted bug</label>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <div class="switches play-actions">
        <button class="btn primary" type="submit" id="play-run">▶ Run</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="play-hunt">Hunt</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="play-replay">Replay</button>
      </div>
      <p class="run-out" id="play-out" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
    <section class="run run-under" id="run" aria-label="The run in the player"></section>
    <div class="run run-under">
      <div class="run-head label"><span>the report</span><span id="report-time"></span></div>
      <p class="run-out" id="report-verdict"></p>
      <div class="report-cols">
        <div class="table-wrap"><table class="run-table" id="report-assertions"></table></div>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table class="run-table" id="report-faults"></table></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p>The playground needs JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  </div>
  <script is:inline type="application/json" id="runs" set:html={JSON.stringify(runs).replace(/</g, "\\u003c")} />
  <p>A red seed is where the work starts: <a href={url("techniques/debugging/")}>From a red seed to the bug</a> walks
    back from the broken invariant to the first wrong event.
    The engine of this page is the crate <a href={url("crates/#moonpool-wasm-demo")}><code>moonpool-wasm-demo</code></a>, compiled to wasm;
    the chapter <a href={url("part4-integration/07-wasm.html")}>Simulation in the Browser</a> explains how.</p>
  <script is:inline type="module" src={url("playground.js")}></script>
</Doc>
